<article class="bg-canvas py-12 md:py-16" aria-label="Read Windows performance information without guessing at a fix">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 text-lg">
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">A high number on a performance screen can look alarming. Before acting on it, record what the computer was doing and whether the reading coincided with the problem you felt. A snapshot is an observation, not a verdict on the machine.</p>
<h2 class="mt-12 mb-5 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink md:text-3xl">Use the built-in Task Manager</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">On Windows 11, press <strong>Ctrl + Shift + Esc</strong> to open Task Manager. Look at the <strong>Processes</strong> and <strong>Performance</strong> views. Microsoft describes Task Manager as a way to inspect CPU, memory and disk activity. <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/experience/performance-optimization/tips-to-improve-pc-performance-in-windows">See Microsoft's performance guidance</a>.</p>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">For this exercise, observe only. Do not choose End task, disable startup items or change priorities. If your screen differs, note that and stop rather than following unfamiliar controls. Closing Task Manager ends the observation; no reset or cleanup is required.</p>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">This is an educational use of a Windows tool, not a claim that every Naked Tech assessment uses one fixed diagnostic procedure.</p>
<h2 class="mt-12 mb-5 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink md:text-3xl">Give the numbers some context</h2>
<div class="mb-8 overflow-x-auto" role="region" aria-label="Read Windows performance information without guessing at a fix reference table" tabindex="0"><table class="w-full border-collapse text-left text-sm md:text-base">
<thead>
<tr>
<th scope="col" class="border border-line bg-surface p-4 font-bold text-ink">Record</th>
<th scope="col" class="border border-line bg-surface p-4 font-bold text-ink">Why it belongs beside the reading</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">The task you were doing</td>
<td class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">“Opening my browser” is more useful than an isolated number.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">When the delay happened</td>
<td class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">Distinguish before, during and after the slow moment.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">The displayed category and value</td>
<td class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">Keep the name and units; do not rename memory as storage.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">Whether the reading changed</td>
<td class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">A brief peak and a continuing pattern are different observations.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">Other work you recognised</td>
<td class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">Note an update or application you saw, without assuming it caused the delay.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">You do not need a universal “good” percentage. Avoid comparing your computer with a different machine doing different work. If a reading appears high, write down the observation and the symptom rather than diagnosing a failed part.</p>
<h2 class="mt-12 mb-5 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink md:text-3xl">Make a short record</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">A fictional example:</p>
<blockquote class="my-6 border-l-4 border-accent pl-5">
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">While opening the application I normally use, I noticed [category and value] in Task Manager. The delay lasted about [time]. After the application opened, the reading [changed/stayed similar/I did not check].</p>
</blockquote>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Use your own values. There is no need to send a screenshot of the whole process list, especially if it reveals private document titles or workplace information. Do not open confidential material just to reproduce a delay.</p>
<h2 class="mt-12 mb-5 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink md:text-3xl">Know what this exercise cannot decide</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">The display alone does not tell you which upgrade to buy, whether the device is secure or whether replacement is worthwhile. If the computer is unresponsive, important files are inaccessible or a recovery prompt appears, stop experimenting and explain that before arranging routine performance help.</p>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Put your observations into the <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="/guides/slow-computer-assessment-notes/">assessment-notes checklist</a>. If the wait happens mainly online, the <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="/guides/slow-computer-or-internet/">computer or internet guide</a> may be the more useful starting point.</p>
